  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-vision-no-vision",
      "text": "A [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)\n(dsh) plugin that gives a **text-only** LLM vision capability!!!"
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "This release targets the DSH **0.2.x** plugin API, and is built and tested\nagainst `dsh 0.2.1-rc.1` (Cordis 4.0.5). The manifest declares\n`engines.dsh: >=0.2.1-rc.1 <0.3.0`, so the launcher refuses to load it on an\nincompatible runtime instead of failing at call time.\n\nPeer packages: `@deepseek-ai/cordis` ^4.0.5,\n`@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` ^0.2.1-rc.1, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` ^0.2.1-rc.1."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```\npnpm dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-vision-no-vision\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "```yaml\n- name: dsh-vision-no-vision\n  config:\n    # Cap for one complete analysis (conversion + model call), in ms.\n    timeoutMs: 3600000\n\nWithout `provider`/`model`, the tool reads the route from the calling\nsession's latest request header, so the image is analyzed by the same model\nthat is driving the conversation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Note",
      "text": "Seriously, it is not a serious plugin 😝. The tool generates an ascii-art from the input image and feed it into the text-only LLM to guess the content."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```\npnpm install\npnpm typecheck\npnpm build\n```\n\nThe keyless smoke test runs the real tool pipeline and LLM runtime against a\nmock adapter:\n\n```\ncd smoke\nnode --import tsx <deepseek-harness-checkout>/vendor/cordis/bin.js\n```"
    }
  ],
  "skipped": []
